// Title: a function whose result a type-directed op decides is refused at each call as "the type '_8144 must be fully known here ... annotate it"
// Command: graphix --check design/review-2026-11-16/repro/x-diagnostics-concrete-required-call.gx
// Expected: the refusal says that f's result (the 'b: Concrete of the str::parse inside it) is
//   undecided at this call and names what to annotate: the binding that takes the result
//   (`let v: i64 = f(1)`, which passes) or f's return type (`|x: i64| -> i64`, which passes).
// Observed: "at line 11, column 1, in: f(1): the type '_8144 must be fully known here, a
//   type-directed operation reads it: annotate it". '_8144 is a raw cell id (the LSP says
//   '_8936 for the same program), no type-directed operation is written at f(1), and "it"
//   names nothing the program holds. Same with json::read in place of str::parse.
let f = |x: i64| str::parse("[x]")$;
f(1)
